{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790334600000-vm-engineer-linker-m2-fixes-r4.claude-sonnet-5.report.md\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '289,500p;1030,1140p'\nrg -n 'direct-store-put|computed-key|yin-def-write|tree-yin-def' test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-09-25 11:10:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-09-25 18:10:00 +0700\nCoding-Agent: claude (in-process subagent, Sonnet 5)\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n\n# M2 gate fix round 4 report\n\nFix (linker.cljc, tree-definition-occurrences): yin/def-derived\ndefinitions are now dropped (obligations retained) when the module\nhas (a) any definition keyed yin/def, direct :vm/store-put included,\nor (b) any yin/def application whose key is not statically a constant\n(anything but two operands, first a literal), via new\ncomputed-yin-def-write? and tree-yin-def-application-query. Rule is\nper module; no cross-module widening. Docstring updated.\n\nTests (linker_test.cljc): a-direct-store-put-of-yin-def-discharges-\nnothing-from-it and a-computed-key-yin-def-write-discharges-nothing-\nfrom-it, each free of any literal yin/def rebinding. Both verified to\nfail (2 failures) with the old guard restored, then pass.\n\nVerification (sequential, mise): JVM 2,059 tests / 180,916 assertions /\n0 failures (baseline 2,057/180,912); Node 1,975 tests / 47,941\nassertions / 0 failures, \"Testing yin.vm.linker-test\" present; Dart\n1,937 passed, All tests passed (cljd-out removed first). cljstyle\ncheck clean. clj-kondo is not installed under mise, so not run.\nASCII, <=80 columns on added lines. No git state changed.\n   289\t(def ^:private tree-occurrence-query\n   290\t  \"`vm/free-names`' free-name query over the row and occurrence\n   291\t   relations, extended to return each occurrence's path (section 4.1):\n   292\t   the same rules, one more find column.\"\n   293\t  '[:find ?name ?path\n   294\t    :in $ $occ % ?root\n   295\t    :where\n   296\t    [$occ ?root ?path ?v]\n   297\t    [?v :variable ?name]\n   298\t    (not (occ-bound? ?root ?path ?name))])\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t(def ^:private tree-definition-query\n   302\t  \"The definition query behind `vm/ast-requirements` (section 4.1): the\n   303\t   `:vm/store-put` rows and the constant-key `yin/def` applications the\n   304\t   macro expander produces (an application of the `yin/def` variable\n   305\t   with exactly two operands, the first a literal), each binding joined\n   306\t   with its binding row's occurrence path -- the definitions scanner\n   307\t   extends an application's path one step past its operands, to the\n   308\t   invocation position (see `tree-definition-occurrences`).\"\n   309\t  '[:find ?key ?path\n   310\t    :in $ $occ ?root\n   311\t    :where\n   312\t    [$occ ?root ?path ?v]\n   313\t    (or-join [?v ?key]\n   314\t             [?v :vm/store-put ?key _]\n   315\t             (and [?v :application ?op ?operands _]\n   316\t                  [?op :variable yin/def]\n   317\t                  [(count ?operands) 2]\n   318\t                  [(nth ?operands 0) ?name-id]\n   319\t                  [?name-id :literal ?key]))])\n   320\t\n   321\t\n   322\t(def ^:private tree-application-query\n   323\t  \"The application-row query over the same relation (section 4.1): one\n   324\t   application site per `:application` row, carried with the row's\n   325\t   operand count -- the site is recorded where the application happens,\n   326\t   which is only after the operands have run.\"\n   327\t  '[:find ?path ?n\n   328\t    :in $ $occ ?root\n   329\t    :where\n   330\t    [$occ ?root ?path ?v]\n   331\t    [?v :application _ ?operands _]\n   332\t    [(count ?operands) ?n]])\n   333\t\n   334\t\n   335\t(defn- tree-row-at\n   336\t  \"The row `path` names from the tree's root, nil when the path leaves\n   337\t   the tree. A step is a `:node` slot's row position or a `[position i]`\n   338\t   pair into a `:nodes` slot's vector (section 6.1).\"\n   339\t  [{:keys [root rows]} path]\n   340\t  (loop [id root, steps (seq path)]\n   341\t    (if (nil? steps)\n   342\t      (get rows id)\n   343\t      (let [row (get rows id)\n   344\t            step (first steps)\n   345\t            child (when row\n   346\t                    (if (vector? step)\n   347\t                      (let [slot (nth row (nth step 0))]\n   348\t                        (when (vector? slot) (nth slot (nth step 1))))\n   349\t                      (nth row step)))]\n   350\t        (recur child (next steps))))))\n   351\t\n   352\t\n   353\t(defn- tree-enclosure\n   354\t  \"Whether the occurrence at `path` lies inside a lambda body, and\n   355\t   whether an `:if` branch or a lambda body encloses it -- section 4.1's\n   356\t   `:in-body?` and `:conditional?`. Each proper prefix of `path` names\n   357\t   the row the next step leaves: a `:lambda`'s body slot is 3, an `:if`'s\n   358\t   branches 3 and 4 (the section 2.3 grammar's own positions).\"\n   359\t  [tree path]\n   360\t  (loop [i 0, in-body? false, conditional? false]\n   361\t    (if (or (and in-body? conditional?) (>= i (count path)))\n   362\t      [in-body? conditional?]\n   363\t      (let [row (tree-row-at tree (subvec path 0 i))\n   364\t            tag (and row (nth row 1))\n   365\t            step (nth path i)]\n   366\t        (recur (inc i)\n   367\t               (or in-body? (and (= :lambda tag) (= 3 step)))\n   368\t               (or conditional?\n   369\t                   (and (= :lambda tag) (= 3 step))\n   370\t                   (and (= :if tag) (or (= 3 step) (= 4 step)))))))))\n   371\t\n   372\t\n   373\t(defn- tree-rows\n   374\t  \"The row and occurrence relations the tree scanners query, with the\n   375\t   tree's root.\"\n   376\t  [tree]\n   377\t  (let [root (:root tree)\n   378\t        db (query/relation (vals (:rows tree)))\n   379\t        occ (query/relation (vm/occurrences tree))]\n   380\t    {:root root, :db db, :occ occ}))\n   381\t\n   382\t\n   383\t(defn- tree-free-name-occurrences\n   384\t  \"Every free `:variable` occurrence of the tree `{:root root :rows {id\n   385\t   row}}` as a section 4.1 record `{:name sym :at [root path] :in-body?\n   386\t   b}`, in the tree's own path order: `vm/free-names`' occurrence rules\n   387\t   wrapped to carry each occurrence's path (section 4.1).\"\n   388\t  [tree]\n   389\t  (let [{:keys [root db occ]} (tree-rows tree)]\n   390\t    (->> (query/collect\n   391\t           (query/q tree-occurrence-query db occ\n   392\t                    vm/occurrence-rules root\n   393\t                    {:fns vm/occurrence-fns}))\n   394\t         (map (fn [[name path]]\n   395\t                (let [[in-body? _] (tree-enclosure tree path)]\n   396\t                  {:name name, :at [root path], :in-body? in-body?})))\n   397\t         (sort-by (comp second :at) path-order)\n   398\t         vec)))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(def ^:private tree-yin-def-application-query\n   402\t  \"Every application of the `yin/def` variable, with its operand ids\n   403\t   (section 4.1): the sites whose key the definition query may not have\n   404\t   read as a constant.\"\n   405\t  '[:find ?path ?operands\n   406\t    :in $ $occ ?root\n   407\t    :where\n   408\t    [$occ ?root ?path ?v]\n   409\t    [?v :application ?op ?operands _]\n   410\t    [?op :variable yin/def]])\n   411\t\n   412\t\n   413\t(defn- computed-yin-def-write?\n   414\t  \"Whether the module has a `yin/def` application whose key is not\n   415\t   statically a constant: any shape but two operands, the first a\n   416\t   literal, may write a name that evaluates to `yin/def`.\"\n   417\t  [{:keys [rows]} db occ root]\n   418\t  (boolean\n   419\t    (some (fn [[_ operands]]\n   420\t            (not (and (= 2 (count operands))\n   421\t                      (= :literal\n   422\t                         (nth (get rows (nth operands 0)) 1)))))\n   423\t          (query/collect\n   424\t            (query/q tree-yin-def-application-query db occ root)))))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t(defn- tree-definition-occurrences\n   428\t  \"Every constant store key the tree binds at module level as a section\n   429\t   4.1 record `{:name key :at [root path] :conditional? b}`: the\n   430\t   store-key query behind `vm/ast-requirements` (`:vm/store-put` rows\n   431\t   and constant-key `yin/def` applications), each binding carried with\n   432\t   its enclosing tags (section 4.1). A `yin/def` application's binding\n   433\t   is recorded at its invocation position -- the application row's own\n   434\t   path extended one step past its two operands, where the walker\n   435\t   applies the operator only after the operands have run -- so a read\n   436\t   inside the value operand precedes the definition and keeps its\n   437\t   obligation, exactly as for application sites (a `:vm/store-put` row\n   438\t   binds at its own execution position and keeps its own path). A\n   439\t   `yin/def` binding further counts as a store only when the operator\n   440\t   provably resolves to the `yin/def` primitive: runtime resolution\n   441\t   checks the active store before the primitives\n   442\t   (`yin.vm.engine/resolve-var`), so once the module's own footprint\n   443\t   binds `yin/def` -- a `:vm/store-put` of the name, an apparent\n   444\t   `yin/def` binding of it, or a `yin/def` application whose key is not\n   445\t   statically a constant (it may evaluate to the name) -- every\n   446\t   apparent definition of the module may instead be a call of the\n   447\t   store's binding, and each\n   448\t   `yin/def`-derived binding is dropped, fail-closed:\n   449\t   the obligations it would have discharged are retained (the\n   450\t   receiver-side half refuses an operator the receiver's own env or\n   451\t   store already binds, as `:shadowed-free`). Proving the primitive\n   452\t   binding against a verified module manifest is an M4 refinement; the\n   453\t   footprint is the whole static proof here, and over-retaining\n   454\t   obligations is always admissible (section 4.1).\"\n   455\t  [tree]\n   456\t  (let [{:keys [root db occ]} (tree-rows tree)\n   457\t        defs (->> (query/collect\n   458\t                    (query/q tree-definition-query db occ root))\n   459\t                  (map (fn [[key path]]\n   460\t                         (let [row (tree-row-at tree path)\n   461\t                               yin-def? (and row\n   462\t                                             (= :application\n   463\t                                                (nth row 1)))\n   464\t                               at-path (if yin-def?\n   465\t                                         (conj path [3 2])\n   466\t                                         path)\n   467\t                               [_ conditional?]\n   468\t                               (tree-enclosure tree at-path)]\n   469\t                           {:name key, :at [root at-path],\n   470\t                            :yin-def? yin-def?,\n   471\t                            :conditional? conditional?})))\n   472\t                  (sort-by (comp second :at) path-order)\n   473\t                  vec)]\n   474\t    (->> (if (or (some (fn [d] (= 'yin/def (:name d))) defs)\n   475\t                 (computed-yin-def-write? tree db occ root))\n   476\t           (filterv (complement :yin-def?) defs)\n   477\t           defs)\n   478\t         (mapv (fn [d] (dissoc d :yin-def?))))))\n   479\t\n   480\t\n   481\t(defn- tree-application-sites\n   482\t  \"Every application row of the tree as a section 4.1 record `{:at\n   483\t   [root path]}` -- one application site at its invocation position: the\n   484\t   row's own path extended one step past its operands, the position at\n   485\t   which the walker applies the operator after evaluating them\n   486\t   (section 4.1), so a definition inside an operand dominates an\n   487\t   application of the enclosing form.\"\n   488\t  [tree]\n   489\t  (let [{:keys [root db occ]} (tree-rows tree)]\n   490\t    (->> (query/collect\n   491\t           (query/q tree-application-query db occ root))\n   492\t         (map (fn [[path n]]\n   493\t                {:at [root (conj path [3 n])]}))\n   494\t         (sort-by (comp second :at) path-order)\n   495\t         vec)))\n   496\t\n   497\t\n   498\t(defn- stack-free-occurrences\n   499\t  \"Every `:load-free` occurrence of a canonical stack instruction vector\n   500\t   as a section 4.1 record `{:name sym :at pc :in-body? b}`, in pc\n  1030\t      (identical? missing bs)\n  1031\t      (refused :absent {:address address})\n  1032\t\n  1033\t      (and budget (> (byte-count bs) budget))\n  1034\t      (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-bytes, :address address})\n  1035\t\n  1036\t      (not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs))\n  1037\t      (refused :address-mismatch {:address address})\n  1038\t\n  1039\t      :else\n  1040\t      (let [value (decoded bs)]\n  1041\t        (if (nil? value)\n  1042\t          (refused :address-mismatch {:address address, :value nil})\n  1043\t          (if-let [defect (row-defect format value)]\n  1044\t            (refused :descriptor-defect\n  1045\t                     {:identity identity, :address address,\n  1046\t                      :defect defect})\n  1047\t            {:value value, :bytes (byte-count bs)}))))))\n  1048\t\n  1049\t\n  1050\t(def default-bounds\n  1051\t  \"The safe finite composition bounds a fetch falls back to where the\n  1052\t   caller supplies none (section 4.2 step 2): generous for every honest\n  1053\t   image the compositions hold, finite for a hostile one, so no fetch\n  1054\t   path walks an unbounded worklist.\"\n  1055\t  {:max-parts 4096, :max-depth 256, :max-bytes 16777216})\n  1056\t\n  1057\t\n  1058\t(defn- bounded\n  1059\t  \"The composition's `bounds` with every bound it left nil (or never\n  1060\t   named) taking `default-bounds`.\"\n  1061\t  [bounds]\n  1062\t  (into default-bounds\n  1063\t        (map (fn [[k v]] [k (or v (get default-bounds k))]))\n  1064\t        (or bounds {})))\n  1065\t\n  1066\t\n  1067\t(defn- enqueue-children\n  1068\t  \"The children of one fetched part that are not already enqueued, each\n  1069\t   paired with its depth, up to the parts budget: the first child beyond\n  1070\t   the remaining `max-parts` is refused `:parts-limit`, naming the bound\n  1071\t   and its own address, before it is fetched (section 4.2). Returns\n  1072\t   `{:queue [[address depth] ...] :fresh [address ...]}` or a refusal.\"\n  1073\t  [child-addrs enqueued depth max-parts]\n  1074\t  (loop [[child & more] (filter (fn [a] (not (contains? enqueued a)))\n  1075\t                                (distinct child-addrs))\n  1076\t         n (count enqueued)\n  1077\t         acc []]\n  1078\t    (cond\n  1079\t      (nil? child)\n  1080\t      {:queue (mapv (fn [a] [a (inc depth)]) acc), :fresh acc}\n  1081\t\n  1082\t      (>= n max-parts)\n  1083\t      (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-parts, :address child})\n  1084\t\n  1085\t      :else\n  1086\t      (recur more (inc n) (conj acc child)))))\n  1087\t\n  1088\t\n  1089\t(defn- fetch-parts\n  1090\t  \"Step 2: the bounded breadth-first worklist from `root-address`\n  1091\t   (section 4.2). `:parts-fn` names the further addresses a fetched\n  1092\t   payload references; the walk enqueues them behind the current one,\n  1093\t   verifies each the same way, and visits each address once. `bounds` is\n  1094\t   the composition's `{:max-parts n :max-depth d :max-bytes b}`, every\n  1095\t   bound finite (`bounded`); exceeding one is `:parts-limit` naming the\n  1096\t   bound and the address at which it was hit. The parts budget is\n  1097\t   enforced at admission and at enqueue time -- a non-positive quota\n  1098\t   refuses the root before it is read, a child beyond the remaining\n  1099\t   budget is refused before it is fetched -- and the byte budget is\n  1100\t   checked before a payload is hashed or decoded. Returns\n  1101\t   `{:parts {address body} :multi? boolean}` or a refusal. `:multi?` is\n  1102\t   the record's own answer to whether the format has parts at all: a\n  1103\t   single-payload format's `:parts-fn` returns nil, a multi-part\n  1104\t   format's a sequence, possibly empty for a leaf row.\"\n  1105\t  [handle format identity root-address bounds]\n  1106\t  (let [{:keys [max-parts max-depth max-bytes]} (bounded bounds)]\n  1107\t    (if-not (pos? max-parts)\n  1108\t      (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-parts, :address root-address})\n  1109\t      (loop [queue [[root-address 0]]\n  1110\t             index 0\n  1111\t             parts {}\n  1112\t             bytes 0\n  1113\t             enqueued #{root-address}\n  1114\t             multi? nil]\n  1115\t        (if (= index (count queue))\n  1116\t          {:parts parts, :multi? (boolean multi?)}\n  1117\t          (let [[address depth] (nth queue index)]\n  1118\t            (cond\n  1119\t              (and max-depth (> depth max-depth))\n  1120\t              (refused :parts-limit {:bound :max-depth, :address address})\n  1121\t\n  1122\t              :else\n  1123\t              (let [res (fetch-one handle format identity address\n  1124\t                                   (when max-bytes (- max-bytes bytes)))]\n  1125\t                (if (refused? res)\n  1126\t                  res\n  1127\t                  (let [value (:value res)\n  1128\t                        bytes' (+ bytes (:bytes res))\n  1129\t                        child-addrs ((:parts-fn format) value)\n  1130\t                        multi?' (if (nil? multi?)\n  1131\t                                  (not (nil? child-addrs))\n  1132\t                                  multi?)\n  1133\t                        enque