{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The direct and computed-key cases are now covered by the guard, but a call through an alias can still write the module’s `yin/def` slot. For example, a lambda can receive the `yin/def` primitive as an argument and call it with the key `yin/def`; that call matches neither new query. A later syntactic `yin/def 'x` is then treated as a guaranteed store. I’m checking whether any contract rules out that path before deciding the gate."}}
